                + "   • Celsius to Absolute Kelvin: K = C + 273.15 = " + str(c_val) + " + 273.15 = " + str(k_val) + " K.\n"
                + "3) [THERMODYNAMIC EVIDENCE]: K >= 0 K enforces the Third Law of Thermodynamics (absolute zero at -273.15 °C), and inverse conversion (F - 32) / 1.8 recovers C = " + str(c_val) + " °C.\n"
                + "4) [EXECUTABLE PURE-PBLANG VERIFICATION]: `convert_temperature_scales(" + str(c_val) + ")` verifies both conversions below.";
